# [UAA] - START - do not let git rewrite line endings
# Upstream declared per-extension end-of-line rules here (eol=lf for
# .h/.cpp/.cs/.md/.sh/CMakeLists.txt, eol=crlf for .bat/.csv/.vcxproj). Those
# rules contradict the contents of the repository they are applied to: five
# files are committed with CRLF in the stored blob while the attribute demands
# LF, so their working copy can never match the index and they read as modified
# forever, on a completely untouched checkout.
#
# On a Windows worktree it is worse. Every file type the patterns do not cover
# (.txt, .fx, .hlsl, .glsl, .json, .py, .cmake, .inl) falls through to
# core.autocrlf, which produces whitespace-only diffs measured in the thousands
# of lines and turns every rebase into a conflict.
#
# So take git out of the loop. '-text' disables end-of-line conversion outright:
# the working tree is byte-for-byte what is stored, nothing is normalised on
# checkout or on commit, on any platform, whatever core.autocrlf happens to be
# set to locally. Line endings become the author's problem, which is where they
# belong.
* -text
# [UAA] - END

*.lib filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.ttf filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.dll filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
